1.explanation:
The key bug-related element is the main Verilog language definition function in highlight.js, specifically within the array provided to the 'contains' property for syntax highlighting rules. The issue is caused by the rule:
{
  className: 'meta',
  begin: '`',
  end: '$',
  ...
}
This rule matches from the backquote to the end of the line, causing the incorrect scope. This rule is defined inside the 'export default function(hljs)' in 'src/languages/verilog.js', which is responsible for highlighting Verilog code. Editing this function (specifically, the meta rule) is required to fix the bug.

2.explanation:
The function 'export default function(hljs)' in 'src/languages/verilog.js' defines the syntax highlighting rules for Verilog. Within this function, the 'meta' rule is specified as:
{
  className: 'meta',
  begin: '`',
  end: '$',
  ...
}
This rule causes everything from a backquote to the end of the line to be captured as 'meta', which is the source of the bug. To fix the issue, the rule for 'meta' needs to be modified so that only the correct part of the line (such as macro identifiers or directives) is highlighted as 'meta', without including the entire line or trailing comments. No classes are present in the file, so only the top-level function is relevant.
